hat value I can add  to them only then I say yes because  Jesus Navas is a community dedicated to  developers only so whenever if some  sponsor is just coming to sell something  or pitch something I just say move  unless and until it is something  valuable same with me if I am NOT able  to add any value to their company my  committee I say no so if you are going  to pick any sponsor please pick it very  carefully it is very important because  your members are very smart they will  understand that you have a paid sponsor  standing on the stage so you need to be  very careful I have said no to many  sponsors and I don't regret because I  know because of that  there is trust of my members few of the  sponsors we have are here out of that  Amazon egghead native scripts are  knowledge partner the good thing is we  keep doing lot of swags and because of  the swags people also get hooked to us  but it is not that every time they will  get swags this is the most tricky part  this is a surprise factor so if you are  coming to our meetup for example this  month you might get or you might not get  so this was always a surprise vector  collaborations collaborations is very  very important if you try to survive on  your own you will not fall long way you  need to learn from and with others it's  very important so when I started jazz  lovers after few months there were a lot  of people who used to attend our  workshop from first event and one day we  just bounce the idea are you interested  in learning something apart from their  Penzias and they said yes so we did an  IOT workshop and we got very good  response and I asked for the feedback  and they shared that now they feel very  happy because they have a skill apart  from their primary skill and they  enjoyed it and after that I realized  that yes it is important if I am a web  developer but I know like Android or iOS  is a fun you never know what will become  your hobby so I started in collaboration  with other committees and other  technologies and this helped my members  as well as me too as an organizer  because I learned what other organizers  are doing how they are way so I was  missing the biggest thing which is code  of conduct in my community while I was  doing a collaboration one of the  organizer actually shared with me that  you should have a code of conduct in  your committee because if you are if  someone is actually troubling you that  code of conduct can help you a lot and  then I said oh yes I forgot and this is  how I learned it by doing the  collaboration by meeting new organizers  so please if you are getting an  opportunity of doing collaboration do it  I am not scared lot of people come to me  and say you are a Chavez script  why are you doing meetup on XYZ I was  like because my members are asking for  it they wanted to learn and grow and so  I feedback always always ask for the  feedback because this is what I believe  feedbacks are your next steps if chairs  lovers is able to come through three  years it just because of we worked on  feedbacks if I am not getting a feedback  I feel that I am doing literally a very  wrong thing  developers are very shy specially in  Delhi and yeah it's very hard to get  feedback it's very hard to make them  talk so the first thing is language most  of the developers there assume that  their English is not gold and all that  so what as an organizer and speaker we  do is we make them comfortable in  speaking in native language it's fine if  you don't know English but we know your  native language and we actually promote  that it lets have a meet-up on the knee  in native language and when I asked for  the feedback I never asked feedback in  direct questions I always asked with  options so that at least the audience  will reply like did you like the  location yes or no would you like to  have the repeat event here yes or no how  was the food and so it and I always  close my session with the open thread if  you like this event please go out spread  the word on social media in your with  your friends in your company if you  don't please write me a personal email I  will look into it so you need to ask for  the feedback because feedback will help  you a lot improve as a result initially  when people were not open to write their  feedback on the meetup page event page  now they are openly going and sharing  the feedback on social media so this is  how you have to do it there would be the  moment when people are not doing it but  you need to push them and just keep  doing it what failed it's not like this  that everything is working first time  nope lot of lot of things lot of places  where I failed my ideas fail and lot of  things failed few of the things as lot  of meetups so  the idea was to have a lot of meter we  will have a lot of members joining us  and as a result we were doing three to  four meetups in a month which was so  hectic for the organizers as well as for  the members because everyone was busy  Monday to Friday in their job and Sunday  coming for the codelab  is very tricky so did this design wave  work so what we started doing is one  Meetup one cinnamon that's it and that  actually helped us a lot  now people were started looking for that  one meetup in a month to meet us  building the best team running our  community at such scale is very tricky  it was just me and my co organizer and  we used to have our full-time job also  so it's like a crazy job we were doing  two jobs I was not able to build the  team because we were looking for the  best people and as a result I was just  ending up following with them but after  a few months I realized I should look  for the self-motivated people who  understand what it takes to be a part of  the committee and as a result now we  have five people who helped me in social  media graphics and everything they take  care of each and everything and I don't  need to do any follow up and anything  they just know because they are  self-motivated and they know what they  want to do what's happened slack this is  the most asked question please have a  whatsapp or slack rope  I left lot of whatsapp group just  because people used to put all the code  on the whatsapp and as a result I got  annoyed and I have to drop that group  slag group it just get died you need to  be there every time doing moderation  breaking the eyes and everything so it  was like I am running offline committee  and I am also maintaining online  community and every time I have to push  the discussion from one place to another  and I was like this is not done this is  what you asked you need to run it I  can't be the organized main person  behind that so these two things doesn't  work for me so I stopped and I kept  everything on my platform which is  Meetup but the second problem where is  diversity in one of the meter we have  few females and then there is only me  then there are few  females and then again it's only me so I  was like in shock because I was hoping  that a lot of females will come because  a female is the front face she is  running the show she knows all the pain  she has taken care of everything but  nope this is not happening  and then I start thinking it is because  the problem I am facing with my family  my friends my society for them it is  much harder because they are just coming  to attend an event they can't explain to  their family why they are going on  weekend for eight hours at the XY place  just to learn something because in  delhi-ncr the most of the parents like  my parents they are like you have a full  set of job you are getting the salary  that's it don't thing beyond that do not  even think of doing something else so I  knew that trouble and I was like what I  can do about this how can I make sure  that those females are actually knowing  that something is happening they are  learning and everything meanwhile if  there was a girl who attended one of my  workshop progressive web app she reached  me on social media she said she has some  doubts and then I started helping her in  making blogs writing writing blogs  making videos and everything and as a  result after three months I get to know  that she actually built her first  progressive web app she presented a  hundred in college our professor lined  it she give a workshop at her college  level then I did and she also got an  internship because of that and and she  actually messaged me that because you  helped and guided me all through on  social media by doing videos blogging in  everything I'm able to do it and then I  realize it's fine if you are not coming  to my Meetup but for me it would be very  wrong if you are reaching me for asking  help online and I'm not doing it I keep  getting a lot of messages from people I  have never met and I'm sure every  speaker get this that hey you don't know  me you never make me but I have seen  your video I have read your blog it  inspired me to do this that and actually  that is what the community is and that  is how Jesus lever is doing we are not  helping everyone who is space because  because I am a girl sorry  and everyone who is reaching me on  social media on my email that we need  help and I'm helping them out so guys if  you are a community organizer if you are  planning to run a committee it's not  just they came into a room and they vent  your relation is done it's also about  support and mentoring them after that  please do it it will make a lot of lot  of difference as a result meetup on  which my group is they actually invited  me two months ago in their headquarters  in here to share my story as well as  they also covered my story that how I do  a meet-up so good thing also happened  with me I hope this helped you a lot too  if your organizer you get some tips if  you are planning you get an idea how you  have to do it the important part is  never ever give up this is my mantra you  never know who you are inspiring guys  you literally never know I when I  started I didn't knew I am actually  helping so many people but when I get  messages I feel so happy that a small  idea of running our meetup now its reach  to this level thank you guys
 

